cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "quant-bench-5070ti: a reproducible quantization and inference benchmark for a 16 GB consumer Blackwell GPU"
message: "If you use these results or this methodology, please cite the repository and state the snapshot date — engine version churn makes any single run a dated snapshot."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "quant-bench-5070ti contributors"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/USER/quant-bench-5070ti"
abstract: >
  A single-card benchmark matrix answering which quantization format and inference engine
  to run on a 16 GB RTX 5070 Ti (Blackwell GB203, sm_120), and what each choice costs.
  Covers GGUF K-quants and i-quants (with an isolated importance-matrix ablation), AWQ,
  GPTQ, FP8, NF4 and EXL3 across llama.cpp, vLLM, ExLlamaV3 and HF Transformers. Quality is
  measured primarily as KL divergence against a cached FP16 reference rather than
  perplexity; latency is derived from per-token arrival timestamps; VRAM is reported as
  four separate quantities including process-level NVML peak; efficiency is reported as
  tokens per joule. Runs are subprocess-isolated, thermally gated and randomly interleaved,
  and OOM is recorded as a result rather than treated as an error.
keywords:
  - quantization
  - llm-inference
  - benchmark
  - gguf
  - awq
  - gptq
  - exl3
  - blackwell
  - sm_120
  - reproducibility
